                <pb facs="0941" n="929" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg929"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0090/2279: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-17">September 17,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received September 17—8:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5785. American interests Far East, exchange. Legation’s 5724, 14th.<anchor n="38"
                        xml:id="d784-f1"/> Foreign Office note September 16 states Japanese Legation
                    Bern note of September 15 quoted following telegram from Japanese Government:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Teia Maru</hi> sailed from Yokohama for Marmagão
                            via Kobe, Shanghai, Hong Kong, Northern San Fernando, Cap St. Jacques
                            and Syonan as scheduled on September 14 at 1 a.m. Safe conduct assured
                            by all belligerents.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
